        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "95012823-9479-5349-bab9-154b3498801d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Felix Avenue, Marcos Highway, Ortigas Avenue Extension, Cainta, National Arts Center, Philippines\n- People: Francisco P. Felix, Imelda Marcos, Ferdinand Marcos\n- Roles: mayor, President, First Lady, politician\n- Topics: road naming, wealth, offshore bank accounts, inauguration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Imelda Marcos inaugurated the National Arts Center.\n- Felix Avenue, also known as Imelda Avenue, is a four-lane major road that connects Marcos Highway to Ortigas Avenue Extension.\n- Felix Avenue is named after Francisco P. Felix, a former mayor of Cainta, and Imelda Marcos.\n- Imelda Marcos was the wife of former Philippine President Ferdinand Marcos and served as First Lady.\n- Imelda Marcos remains one of the richest politicians in the Philippines through collections of clothing, artwork, and jewelry, along with money in offshore bank accounts under the pseudonym \"Jane Ryan\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
